WEBVTT - Junior Astronaut Mission Trainer (JAMT) Demo Video Captions
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Welcome to the Junior Astronaut Mission Trainer,

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
created by Team LYTEN for the 2026 NASA Space Apps Challenge.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.000
JAMT teaches children aged 7 to 12 how to command a deep-space outpost

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
through consequential systems thinking where every choice has a real cost.

00:20.000 --> 00:25.000
More crew completes tasks faster, but breathes more oxygen and eats more food.

00:25.000 --> 00:30.000
Across six tactical steps, players balance four vital life-support meters:

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Power, Air and Water, Crew Health, and Food, animated by procedural 3D.

00:35.000 --> 00:41.000
Suddenly, space weather strikes! This isn't random fiction.

00:41.000 --> 00:47.000
JAMT pulls real solar flare and CME data directly from NASA's CCMC DONKI database.

00:47.000 --> 00:52.000
The flare class, peak time, and active region are authentic records.

00:52.000 --> 00:57.000
Commanders must decide under pressure: retreat, rush work, or overcharge shields.

00:57.000 --> 01:03.000
On Mars, NASA's true speed-of-light communication delay takes effect.

01:03.000 --> 01:10.000
Mission Control's answer won't arrive for 14 minutes, demanding autonomy.

01:10.000 --> 01:17.000
Our core rule is transparency. Press L to activate the Data Loupe.

01:17.000 --> 01:25.000
Every number is tagged REAL DATA with direct NASA sources, or GAME RULE for balance.

01:25.000 --> 01:32.000
The in-game NASA Data Passport lets kids and teachers explore verified science,

01:32.000 --> 01:40.000
from OSDR plant biology studies to genuine Apollo and Artemis references.

01:40.000 --> 01:45.000
For evaluators, dedicated Judge Mode allows one-click demo runs,

01:45.000 --> 01:50.000
historical storm replays from May 2024, and the live Science Map.

01:50.000 --> 01:55.000
100% web-based, procedural audio, zero trackers, and fully offline capable.

01:55.000 --> 02:00.000
Junior Astronaut Mission Trainer: empowering the next generation of explorers!
